{
    "word": "apothegm",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "a7b3f5a6-c853-3886-86db-0cadc910b99d",
                "word": "apothegm",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "2bfff509-f946-4d05-ace7-c5d9febc06c6",
                        "entry_id": "a7b3f5a6-c853-3886-86db-0cadc910b99d",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "apothegms"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b5906e88-53dd-3353-b042-d05aed021315",
                        "entry_id": "a7b3f5a6-c853-3886-86db-0cadc910b99d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A short, witty, instructive saying; an aphorism or maxim."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6c36c48a-bcde-4340-b291-329848671fd5",
                                "sense_id": "b5906e88-53dd-3353-b042-d05aed021315",
                                "text": "Every glaſs of wine, or bit almoſt, that I committed to my mouth, ſhe uſhered thither with ſome Apothegm or other: the whole ſeries, indeed, of her diſcourſe, was compoſed of nothing but reaſon or wit, which made me admire her; which ſhe eaſily underſtood, I perceived by her ſmiles, when ſhe obſerved me gaping, as it were, when ſhe ſpoke, as if I would have eaten up her Words."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "62d2e6f6-432f-406c-a5dd-0b3946317270",
                                "sense_id": "b5906e88-53dd-3353-b042-d05aed021315",
                                "text": "The account which he [James Ferguson] himself gives of these observations is exceedingly interesting, and strikingly brings out the ingenuity of his mind, and his determination to allow no difficulties of circumstances to stand in his way. [...] Thus we are reminded of the apothegm that where there's a will there's a way—an apothegm which has found illustration in every department of effort, but nowhere more frequently than in the progress of science and art."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a15ba2b0-21ba-4a2a-8ecd-df4e70a4a56b",
                                "sense_id": "b5906e88-53dd-3353-b042-d05aed021315",
                                "text": "\"You are too wonderful!\" he would say. \"How do you find time for everything?\"\nShe rejoined with the apophthegm that made the rounds of Riseholme next day.\n\"My dear, it is just busy people that have time for everything.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "de7197ee-618f-4469-ab72-2350f6ae6485",
                                "sense_id": "b5906e88-53dd-3353-b042-d05aed021315",
                                "text": "For the gods have withheld from the barbarians the light of discretion, as that their poetry is not, like ours, full of choice apophthegms and useful maxims, but is all of love and war."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "afd52f3f-ba56-4604-be6f-5d14d48b2d67",
                                "sense_id": "b5906e88-53dd-3353-b042-d05aed021315",
                                "text": "The gnomic belief that the world is conditioned by love is no idle apothegm."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7fb08967-bb23-4c60-b8ec-1a009d03223a",
                                "sense_id": "b5906e88-53dd-3353-b042-d05aed021315",
                                "text": "Which means roughly that business keeps one safe from love—ominous talk when one’s lover is a courtesan. I hoped that it was just another literary conceit I ought to know. (It is, I later learned, an apothegm by Ovid.)"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0890304e-5f14-4d0a-a5f1-d62b3227806d",
                        "source_entry_id": "a7b3f5a6-c853-3886-86db-0cadc910b99d",
                        "source_sense_id": "b5906e88-53dd-3353-b042-d05aed021315",
                        "source_sense_description": "A short witty instructive saying",
                        "target_lang_word": "apophtegme",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "apophtegme",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "04b7383c-c623-3394-bced-b9f2cda01907",
                                        "entry_id": "943ffd9b-eaa6-3f67-8402-04f336737572",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Parole mémorable, maxime, adage, aphorisme."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4608d686-a8a9-4d3a-a778-a0faa4a0862d",
                                                "sense_id": "04b7383c-c623-3394-bced-b9f2cda01907",
                                                "text": "Parmi les traités de morale qui eurent le plus de vogue au moyen-âge, quelques-uns étaient, pour le fonds, purement ou presque purement païens, comme les prétendus apophtegmes de Caton, la Consolation de Boëce."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "98cef236-d7e5-4469-b64c-535746636276",
                                                "sense_id": "04b7383c-c623-3394-bced-b9f2cda01907",
                                                "text": "Croyez-en un vieux philosophe qui connaît les choses dont il parle et a fait la rude expérience des apophtegmes qu’il émet."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "62b76101-cd5b-4f5d-b6e5-924ecb5c442a",
                                                "sense_id": "04b7383c-c623-3394-bced-b9f2cda01907",
                                                "text": "Seulement le symbole rendait plus visible le sens caché, et Blazius, à qui la langue démangeait, se mit à moraliser sur ce thème avec force citations, apophtegmes et maximes que ses rôles de pédant lui suppéditaient en la mémoire."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f83cd6f3-c8fc-465d-8896-c9a4ab8dec7d",
                                                "sense_id": "04b7383c-c623-3394-bced-b9f2cda01907",
                                                "text": "La position internationale du Mexique peut être synthétisée par l’apophtegme de Benito Juarez : « Le respect du droit d’autrui — aussi bien chez les individus que parmi les nations — est la paix. »"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9f02cf6d-28a2-4cfc-bb32-f6e602647fe6",
                                                "sense_id": "04b7383c-c623-3394-bced-b9f2cda01907",
                                                "text": "Les organisateurs eux-mêmes, issus de l’Institut de twittérature comparée (ITC), reconnaissent que cette micro-littérature s’inscrit dans « le prolongement oulipien de la maxime, du proverbe, de l’apophtegme ou du haïku »."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4e444658-c9e2-38a9-8564-634caca2c0c8",
                                        "entry_id": "943ffd9b-eaa6-3f67-8402-04f336737572",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Petit récit à vocation morale ou spirituelle, fable, parabole."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "85cc71f1-2524-4236-a1b7-5dc74b07e8e3",
                                                "sense_id": "4e444658-c9e2-38a9-8564-634caca2c0c8",
                                                "text": "En y réfléchissant, on comprend mieux pourquoi les Pères du désert employaient souvent la technique des apophtegmes, sortes de petits récits assortis de sentences, pour se faire comprendre et transmettre leur expérience spirituelle."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d6ccb740-e884-475f-91bd-29af149a25f2",
                        "source_entry_id": "a7b3f5a6-c853-3886-86db-0cadc910b99d",
                        "source_sense_id": "b5906e88-53dd-3353-b042-d05aed021315",
                        "source_sense_description": "A short witty instructive saying",
                        "target_lang_word": "Apophthegma",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
